= Practice Questions — Part 1 (Q1 to Q5)

#mcq(1, [During the conversion of milk into curd, Lactic Acid Bacteria (LAB) induce biochemical transformations that enhance both curd texture and human health. Which statement correctly identifies a primary nutritional benefit imparted by LAB?], (
  [They significantly enhance the nutritional value of milk by synthesizing substantial amounts of Vitamin B#sub[12]],
  [They ferment lactose into ascorbic acid, significantly increasing the Vitamin C content of the curd],
  [They degrade toxic casein proteins into synthetic glycogen granules stored in the intestinal mucosa],
  [They eliminate all resident gastric flora by secreting high concentrations of concentrated hydrochloric acid],
))
#solution(1, [When milk is converted into curd by Lactic Acid Bacteria (LAB), predominantly _Lactobacillus_, the bacteria ferment lactose into lactic acid, which coagulates and partially digests casein milk proteins. In addition to creating curd, this fermentation significantly enhances the nutritional value of the milk by increasing its *Vitamin B#sub[12]* content. LAB also play a protective role in the human stomach by checking pathogenic microbes.], answer: [A])

#mcq(2, [The puffed-up, spongy appearance observed during the leavening of bread dough and South Indian idli/dosa batter is primarily caused by:], (
  [The evaporation of ethanol vapors during room temperature dough storage],
  [The generation of carbon dioxide ($C O_2$) gas by anaerobic microbial respiration trapped in the dough],
  [The mechanical churning of gluten proteins during high-speed industrial kneading],
  [The secretion of proteolytic enzymes that digest starch into insoluble nitrogen gas],
))
#solution(2, [Bread dough rises and develops a soft, spongy texture due to alcoholic fermentation mediated by Baker's yeast, *_Saccharomyces cerevisiae_*. The yeast metabolizes sugars to produce ethanol and *carbon dioxide ($C O_2$)* gas. As the $C O_2$ bubbles expand and become trapped within the gluten network, they cause the characteristic puffed-up appearance of the dough.], answer: [B])

#mcq(3, [Which of the following organic acids is correctly matched with its industrial microbial source organism?], (
  [Citric acid — _Acetobacter aceti_ (Bacterium)],
  [Acetic acid — _Clostridium butylicum_ (Fungus)],
  [Citric acid — _Aspergillus niger_ (Fungus)],
  [Butyric acid — _Lactobacillus_ (Yeast)],
))
#solution(3, [The precise verified NCERT pairings are: (1) *Citric acid* is produced by the filamentous fungus *_Aspergillus niger_*; (2) *Acetic acid* is produced by the bacterium *_Acetobacter aceti_*; (3) *Butyric acid* is produced by the obligate anaerobic bacterium *_Clostridium butylicum_*; and (4) *Lactic acid* is produced by the bacterium *_Lactobacillus_*. Therefore, option C is correctly matched.], answer: [C])

#mcq(4, [Statins, a premier class of pharmacological agents prescribed globally to lower serum cholesterol, function biochemically by which mechanism?], (
  [Competitively inhibiting the enzyme HMG-CoA reductase responsible for cholesterol synthesis],
  [Directly hydrolyzing dietary cholesterol into bile pigments in the duodenal lumen],
  [Irreversibly binding to low-density lipoproteins and precipitating them into the gallbladder],
  [Allosterically activating pancreatic lipases to accelerate the excretion of fatty acids],
))
#solution(4, [Statins are bioactive molecules produced by the red mold yeast *_Monascus purpureus_*. Statins act as *competitive inhibitors* of the enzyme *HMG-CoA reductase*, which catalyzes the rate-limiting step in the hepatic biosynthesis of cholesterol. By occupying the active site of HMG-CoA reductase, statins prevent the conversion of HMG-CoA to mevalonate, effectively lowering blood cholesterol levels.], answer: [A])

#mcq(5, [Biochemical Oxygen Demand (BOD) is a standard regulatory parameter evaluated in wastewater analytics. Which statement regarding BOD is scientifically accurate?], (
  [A high BOD value signifies that water is completely purified and safe for drinking],
  [BOD evaluates the quantity of inorganic heavy metals settled gravitationally in the grit chamber],
  [BOD is completely independent of the quantity of dissolved organic matter present in sewage],
  [A high BOD value directly indicates a high concentration of organic matter and high polluting potential],
))
#solution(5, [Biochemical Oxygen Demand (BOD) refers to the amount of dissolved oxygen required by aerobic microbes to oxidize all biodegradable organic matter in one liter of water. Because microbes consume oxygen in direct proportion to the quantity of organic substrate present, a *high BOD directly signifies heavy organic pollution and high polluting potential*. Once secondary treatment successfully reduces the organic load, the BOD drops significantly.], answer: [D])

