= Practice Questions — Part 3 (Q11 to Q15)

#mcq(11, [The large, conspicuous holes observed in traditional Swiss cheese are carved out by which microorganism producing copious amounts of carbon dioxide ($C O_2$)?], (
  [_Propionibacterium freudenreichii_ subsp. _shermanii_],
  [_Penicillium roqueforti_],
  [_Saccharomyces cerevisiae_],
  [_Streptococcus thermophilus_],
))
#solution(11, [The large holes characteristic of Swiss cheese are produced by the bacterium *_Propionibacterium freudenreichii_ subsp. _shermanii_*. During the slow ripening process, this bacterium ferments lactic acid to produce propionic acid and large volumes of *carbon dioxide ($C O_2$)* gas. As bubbles of $C O_2$ accumulate and escape through the firm cheese matrix, they carve out the conspicuous holes.], answer: [A])

#mcq(12, [Commercially bottled fruit juices purchased from retail stores appear sparkling and crystal-clear compared to cloudy homemade fruit juices because industrial juices are treated with:], (
  [Lipases and Amylases],
  [Cellulases and Ligases],
  [Pectinases and Proteases],
  [Streptokinase and Lysozyme],
))
#solution(12, [Fresh homemade fruit juices appear cloudy and turbid due to suspended insoluble plant cell-wall pectins and proteinaceous colloids. Industrial fruit juice manufacturers treat the raw pressed juice with the hydrolytic enzymes *Pectinases* and *Proteases*. These enzymes hydrolyze the structural pectin and protein polymers into soluble fragments, rendering bottled juices crystal-clear.], answer: [C])

#mcq(13, [Cyclosporin A is a cyclic non-ribosomal peptide widely administered in organ transplantation as an immunosuppressive agent. It is extracted commercially from which organism?], (
  [_Monascus purpureus_ (Yeast)],
  [_Streptococcus_ (Bacterium)],
  [_Trichoderma polysporum_ (Fungus)],
  [_Aspergillus niger_ (Fungus)],
))
#solution(13, [*Cyclosporin A* is an 11-amino-acid cyclic peptide isolated from the soil fungus *_Trichoderma polysporum_*. It acts as a powerful *immunosuppressive agent* by inhibiting calcineurin phosphatase and suppressing T-lymphocyte activation. It is administered to patients undergoing organ transplantation (e.g., kidney, liver, heart) to prevent host immune rejection of the grafted organ.], answer: [C])

#mcq(14, [Baculoviruses belonging to the genus _Nucleopolyhedrovirus_ (NPV) are considered premier biocontrol agents in Integrated Pest Management (IPM) because they:], (
  [Produce broad-spectrum toxins that kill all insects, fish, and birds in the agricultural zone],
  [Are obligate plant parasites that stimulate root development and mineral phosphorus uptake],
  [Infect human pathogens in domestic sewage to reduce biochemical oxygen demand],
  [Are strictly species-specific and narrow-spectrum, exhibiting zero toxicity to mammals, birds, fish, or non-target insects],
))
#solution(14, [Baculoviruses of the genus *_Nucleopolyhedrovirus_* (NPV) are celebrated in sustainable agro-ecology because they are strictly *species-specific and narrow-spectrum insecticidal pathogens*. They infect specific arthropods without causing any harm to plants, mammals, birds, fish, or non-target insects such as bees and predatory beetles, making them ideal for Integrated Pest Management (IPM).], answer: [D])

#mcq(15, [In terrestrial ecosystems, many plant families establish a mutualistic mycorrhizal association with the fungal genus _Glomus_. What critical nutritional benefit does the fungal partner provide to the host plant?], (
  [Direct fixation of atmospheric elemental dinitrogen into ammonium ions],
  [Absorption of phosphorus from the soil and its translocation into the host plant],
  [Synthesis of broad-spectrum antibiotics that permanently sterilize the leaf phyllosphere],
  [Excretion of massive quantities of ethyl alcohol that protects roots from freezing],
))
#solution(15, [In a mycorrhizal mutualism, such as those formed by the fungal genus *_Glomus_*, the extensive fungal mycelial network acts as an extension of the plant's root system, absorbing *phosphorus* from the soil and translocating it directly to the host plant. Additionally, mycorrhizal associations confer heightened resistance to root-borne pathogens and enhance tolerance to drought and salinity.], answer: [B])

